course: dictionary
lesson: 12840
title: Encircling: surrounding on every side
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Encircling comes from the word circle. To encircle something is to form a circle around it, so it is surrounded on all sides. The -ing ending shows that the action is happening: «The encircling hills kept the little town safe from the wind.»
explain: Use the clues around the word. «Armies encircled the city for six weeks.» An army does not stand on just one side of a city; it makes a ring around it. Try your meaning in the sentence: "Armies surrounded the city for six weeks" still makes sense, so encircling must mean surrounding.
explain: Encircling can also mean moving round in a circle. «The dog was encircling the tree, chasing its tail.» The dog is not standing still around the tree. It is running round and round it. Always check: does your meaning fit the sentence?
fact: Encircling means forming a circle around something, so it is surrounded on all sides.
fact: Encircling can also mean moving around something in a circle.
fact: «The encircling hills» means the hills that surround a town or valley.
fact: In history, an army that encircles a city surrounds it so that the people inside are cut off.
fact: In a story, «the encircling dark» makes a place feel dangerous, because there seems to be no way out.
exercise: «The encircling hills kept the little town safe from the wind.» What does encircling mean here? | Flying high above the town | * Surrounding the town on all sides | Hidden under the town | Moving quickly past the town
exercise: «The children were encircling the bonfire, holding hands.» What were the children doing? | Running away from the bonfire | Sleeping beside the bonfire | * Forming a ring around the bonfire | Lighting the bonfire
exercise: In art class, Maya is encircling a star with a red pencil. What is she doing? | * Drawing a ring around the star | Hiding the star | Cutting the star out | Colouring the star in
test: «Armies were encircling the city for weeks.» What does this tell us? | The city was being built | The armies had gone home | The city was empty | * The city was surrounded on all sides
test: Which phrase means hills that surround a town? | the hilly path | * the encircling hills | the hill walkers | the steep climb
exam: «The encircling dark made the forest feel dangerous.» Which word best means the same as encircling here? | Singing | Sleeping | Shining | * Surrounding
